Orders\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/nominations-appointments/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Nominations &amp; Appointments\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNominations &amp; Appointments\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/presidential-memoranda/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Presidential Memoranda\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPresidential Memoranda\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/proclamations/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Proclamations\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tProclamations\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Fact Sheets\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The attacks on President Donald J. Trump’s public service announcements are highly dishonest.</strong> The announcements are very clearly not campaign ads; President Trump is not on the ballot and there is no call to action. Instead, the announcements are a reminder for Americans to love their country and know why it’s worth defending — at home, at the border, and abroad.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That’s not partisanship — that’s a government that still believes in the country it serves.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-administrations-of-both-parties-have-used-public-service-announcements-to-explain-policy-and-make-the-case-for-the-nation-s-direction\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Administrations of both parties have used public service announcements to explain policy and make the case for the nation’s direction:</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The G.W. Bush Administration ran a <a href=\"https://www.gao.gov/products/b-302504#:~:text=Similar%20to%20the,for%20more%20information.\">national television campaign</a> explaining the Medicare Prescription Drug, Improvement, and Modernization Act to seniors. It also <a href=\"https://www.ourmidland.com/news/article/White-House-Airing-Super-Bowl-Ads-7080786.php\">bought</a> <a href=\"https://www.nydailynews.com/2002/01/31/white-house-spends-34m-for-super-ads/\">Super Bowl airtime</a> for anti-drug and anti-terrorism <a href=\"https://www.wltx.com/article/news/nation/youtube-showcases-bushs-anti-drug-campaign/101-382795056\">public service announcements</a>.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Obama Administration used national advertising to promote <a href=\"https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/finance/obama-administration-will-advertise-healthcare-subsidies-to-combat-perceptions-of-unaffordability-of-aca-health-plans/\">Obamacare subsidies</a> and <a href=\"https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/regulatory/obama-admin-to-blast-tv-social-media-ads-before-open-enrollment\">open enrollment</a>, and a <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2015/05/19/us/critics-hear-epas-voice-in-public-comments.html#:~:text=The%20White%20House,Instagram%2C%20Vine%2C%20Pinterest.%E2%80%9D\">digital campaign</a> to sell its Waters of the United States rule.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Biden Administration poured hundreds of millions of dollars into “<a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/04/01/biden-pro-vaccine-tv-ads/\">We Can Do This</a>” — television, digital, radio, and print spots — to drive a nationwide public health message.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>It’s not just modern Administrations. President Woodrow Wilson’s <a href=\"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/history/how-woodrow-wilsons-propaganda-machine-changed-american-journalism-180963082/\">Committee on Public Information</a> <a href=\"https://wwichangedus.org/topics/selling-the-war/\">used</a> posters, films, and speakers to rally the country. President Franklin D. Roosevelt’s <a href=\"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9182-consolidating-certain-war-information-functions-into-office-war\">Office of War Information</a> <a href=\"https://www.marshallfoundation.org/articles-and-features/marshall-and-the-office-of-war-information/\">produced</a> films, radio, and posters to promote the war effort.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When prior Administrations utilized the airwaves, it was <a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/biden-administration-formally-launches-national-vaccination-outreach-campaign-n1262236\">called</a> “public education.” When this Administration promotes pride in our country, many of those same voices <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/09/24/ad-boosting-trump-paid-by-taxpayers-airing-la-chicago/\">call it</a> “propaganda.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Patriotism isn’t partisan.</strong> These public service announcements are unapologetically American, clearly disclosed, and aimed at the country — not a line on the ballot.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/09/presidential-public-service-announcements-are-nothing-new/\">Presidential Public Service Announcements Are Nothing New</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
